From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:43:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2769/2769] arm64: dts: qcom: surface-laptop8: Turn off the
 PMIC RTC

The tree set qcom,uefi-rtc-info on the PMK8850 RTC, but this firmware
has no RTCInfo variable, so rtc-pm8xxx failed to probe with -ENOENT and
the laptop had no RTC. Without the property the driver would register
the bare counter, which counts from when the PMIC was first powered
(about 197 days on this laptop), and Linux would read a date in 1970.

The laptop keeps its time in SAM, which rtc-surface drives. Turn the
PMIC RTC off so SAM's clock is rtc0 and sets the system time at boot.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts     | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
index 331b61d..09605da 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
@@ -767,8 +767,11 @@
 };
 
 &pmk8850_rtc {
-	qcom,uefi-rtc-info;
-	qcom,no-alarm;
+	/*
+	 * The firmware keeps no UEFI offset for this counter; the time is
+	 * kept by SAM (rtc-surface).
+	 */
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &remoteproc_adsp {
